,"television producer"],"debut":"2002","agencies":[],"groups":[{"id":"Q24909324","name":"Boys Generally Asian","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/davidchoimusic/","x":"https://x.com/davidchoimusic","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/451b12b6-5505-4c30-96a9-5fbe2d15c3d4"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"David Choi is an American singer, songwriter, producer, music composer, entrepreneur, YouTuber, and a member of parody K-pop group BgA based in Los Angeles. He has worked with companies such as Kellogg's, Starburst, the American Cancer Society, General Electric, Samsung, and J. C. Penney. David is also the founder and CEO of CHOIS MUSIC, INC, an independent music label, publisher, rights management service provider, that helps to manage and administer music catalogs on behalf of their clients. Choi released his debut album, Only You, in October 2008. His second album, By My Side, was released on May 19, 2010, and his third album, Forever and Ever was released on October 25, 2011.","title":"David Choi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Choi"}},"Q18907394":{"id":"Q18907394","name":"GSoul","ko":"","birthName":"김지현","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["G.Soul","Golden"],"birth":"1988-06-16","death":"","birthplace":"","nationality":["United States"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer"],"debut":"2015","agencies":[{"name":"JYP Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q483238","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/g_theprince/","x":"https://x.com/GSOULplanet","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/b37f37af-a86c-4794-b4b0-115e5d515718"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/%EC%95%84%EB%A6%AC%EB%9E%91TV%2C_%EC%95%84%EC%9E%84%EB%9D%BC%EC%9D%B4%EB%B8%8C%2C_%EC%A7%80%EC%86%8C%EC%9A%B8_-_14%EC%9D%BC_%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_2-1.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%95%84%EB%A6%AC%EB%9E%91TV,_%EC%95%84%EC%9E%84%EB%9D%BC%EC%9D%B4%EB%B8%8C,_%EC%A7%80%EC%86%8C%EC%9A%B8_-_14%EC%9D%BC_%EB%B0%A9%EC%86%A1_2-1.jpg","author":"아리랑TV","license":"CC BY 4.0"},"bio":{"text":"Kim Ji-hyun, professionally known as Golden or G.Soul, is a South Korean singer-songwriter. He first made his debut under JYP Entertainment with the release of his EP Coming Home on January 19, 2015. On June 6, 2017, it was revealed that he left JYP and would be joining H1ghr Music. On December 2, 2019, it was announced by H1ghr Music that G.Soul would change his name to Golden, named after a song by Jill Scott. In 2020, he won the third season of The Voice of Korea. On January 11, 2021, he announced via Instagram Stories that he would be changing his name back to G.Soul.","title":"G.Soul","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G.Soul"}},"Q21012418":{"id":"Q21012418","name":"Jeong Ye-in","ko":"정예인","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":["Chŏng Yein","Yein","Jung Yein"],"birth":"1998-06-04","death":"","birthplace":"Incheon","nationality":["South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["singer","actor"],"debut":"2014","agencies":[{"name":"Woollim Entertainment","korean":true,"id":"Q50596","start":"","end":""}],"groups":[{"id":"Q18437003","name":"Lovelyz","start":"","end":""}],"links":{"instagram":"https://www.instagram.com/happpy_yein/","youtube":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCSN5ywQds0YaUywVSql1C6Q","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/b5c0209a-2068-4cea-b966-896d4b9e03dd"},"photo":null,"bio":{"text":"Jeong Ye-in, known mononymously as Yein, is a South Korean singer and actress. She is a member of the South Korean girl group Lovelyz.","title":"Jeong Ye-in","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeong_Ye-in"}},"Q26689986":{"id":"Q26689986","name":"Mark Lee","ko":"마크 (1999년)","birthName":"","birthNameEn":"","aliases":[],"birth":"1999-08-02","death":"","birthplace":"Toronto","nationality":["Canada","South Korea"],"height":null,"occupations":["rapper","singer","son